<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belozersk</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Beloozero</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belozersk, known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> as Beloozero, is a town on the southern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-beloye">Lake Beloye</a> in Vologda Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> names it under 862 as the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sineus">Sineus</a>, one of the legendary Varangian brothers. It was the centre of a northern principality and a base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a>, and passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in the 14th century. Its earthen ramparts of the 15th century survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belozersk.jpg" alt="Belozersk" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Astrid123 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChurchOfEpiphany.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
